, "content": "<strong>Darlan:</strong> Wow. I'm sure that the statistics department will feel comfortable with that.</p>"}], "selected": 0, "correct": true, "id": 7, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "<strong>Mary:</strong> Of course. Finally, the last benefit is that "}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 8, "text": ""}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": "a quick data validation is going to reduce the risk of data loss.</p>"}], "selected": 0, "correct": true, "id": 9, "text": ""}], "id": 0}], "type": "SLS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Next month, we are carrying out a data validation process. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Read the text and select all the sentences about "}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "id": 0}, {"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "RSLT", "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}], "id": 11}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob08re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Let's plan how to lead the validation process. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 12}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n5le02ob08re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob08re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Mariana</strong>: Dan, you used to work for TeCHno industries, right?<br /><strong>Dan</strong>: Yes, I used to be one of the professionals that carried out validation processes on the different company&rsquo;s systems.<br /><strong>Mariana</strong>: I am starting my new job this week. What can you tell me about data validation?<br /><strong>Dan</strong>: I can remember that there used to be two parts to any validation method. The first one, the data screening, would implement a series of different algorithms and codes to screen all the data values that could be doubtful, resulting in a report of the data validity. The second one, the data verification, would retake the suspicious values and decide what the proper action would be for each one. In other words, a professional will decide which and how to address the values by validating, rejecting, replacing or fixing them."}, {"time": "49500", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob08re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Mariana</strong>: Great, what about the measured parameters check?<br /><strong>Dan</strong>: It is one of the validation routines that will measure, through three different tests, various parameters before the values are incorporated in the data base. The range test is going to compare the data with pre-stablished limits and assess it in different criteria. The relational test, is going to corroborate that improbable situations of the real world are not included in the data without proper verification. Finally, the trend test is going to analyze the changes that data, and some criteria, suffer through an established period of time."}, {"time": "89500", "image": "enpe8n5le02ob08re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Mariana</strong>: Why did the data validation use to be so important?<br /><strong>Dan</strong>: Well, it used to be and still is really important. Its main objective is to detect and fix, on the shortest notice, erroneous data as well as to identify their cause in order to ensure the proper operation of applications, and avoid any similar flaws in future projects."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n5le02ob08re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}